==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|grabanan|lang=non}}, whence also Old English {{term|grafan|lang=ang}} (English {{term|grave#Etymology 2|grave}}), Old Saxon {{term|bigraban|bigraƀan|lang=osx}}, Dutch {{term|graven|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|graban|lang=goh}} (German {{term|graben}}), Gothic {{term|𐌲𐍂𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽|tr=graban|sc=Goth}}.

===Verb===
{{infl|non|verb}}

# to [[dig]]
# to [[bury]]
# to [[engrave]]
# to [[enquire]] (also in middle voice: [[grafask]])
# {{impersonal|lang=is}} to cause the formation of [[pus]] (in sth); [[suppurate]]

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
* Danish: [[grave#Danish|grave]]
* Faroese: [[grava#Faroese|grava]]
* Icelandic: [[#Icelandic|grafa]]
{{mid2}}
